            0.495
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 151**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.506,
            0.843,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": "**2. Use the points on the circles and/or their centres to form isosceles and equilateral triangles. The circles are of the same size.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.562,
            0.464,
            0.73
          ],
          "content": "",
