        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.746,
            0.169,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.765,
            0.879,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": "Take points $\\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{C}_{1}, \\mathrm{C}_{2}, \\mathrm{C}_{3} \\ldots$ on the circle with centre B. The triangles ABC, $\\mathrm{AC_{1}B, AC_{2}B, \\cdots}$ are isosceles triangle. Similarly for points $\\mathrm{D}_{1}, \\mathrm{D}_{2}, \\mathrm{D}_{3} \\ldots \\Delta \\mathrm{ADB},$ $\\Delta \\mathrm{AD}_{1}\\mathrm{B},\\Delta \\mathrm{AD}_{2}\\mathrm{B},\\ldots$ are isosceles triangles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.823,
            0.557,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": "$\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C }$ and $\\Delta \\mathrm { A D B }$ are equilateral triangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.842,
            0.594,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": "Similarly it can be done for the other figure."
